            <ArticleTitle>[Appearance on effort of an image of a sub-epicardial lesion in the absence of signs of myocardial necrosis. Clinical, electrocardiographic and coronographic studies of 10 cases].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>401-22</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A clinical, electrocardiographic and coronarographic study of ten cases shows that surelevation of ST-segment during exercise (without any signs of infarction) correspond to very different clinical situations of anatomical state of coronary vessels, occurrence of coronary spasm and evolution of the ischemic disease. &quot;Inversed coronary Insufficiency&quot; is proposed to design this syndrome. Practical recommandations are formulated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
